Patch 2025: per-draw fragment program hash, size and texture-unit mask from one memoised walk (SHADER_HASH_MEMO=0 off).

Every draw walked its fragment program three times (rsx_fp_program_size, rsx_fp_code_hash with a serial multiply per byte,
rsx_fp_texture_units for the shadow descriptors): about 12% of the drawing thread in a J-Stars fight. The three answers depend
only on the instruction blocks rsx_fp_code_hash visits, so one walk copies those blocks into a 64-bit key and a small per-thread
table returns the stored answers when the same blocks come back (a hit compares the blocks byte for byte, so the result is
exact). Keyed by content, not address: J-Stars copies each draw's program into a ring. After the v0.15 port's
SHADER_HASH_MEMO.

Tested (US disc, Free Battle, same scripted route, same build): game flips per second over the same 100 s of the fight 13.1
with it, 11.8 with SHADER_HASH_MEMO=0.

